# The acceptance script's run directory. It holds that run's build logs, its
# synthesized stand-in base and the evidence copies its rows read back — scratch
# from a deployment, not a shipped artifact. Ignored here so a consumer who
# clones the catalogue never receives somebody else's verification output, and so
# a re-run cannot re-add it: `scripts/verify-harness-layer.sh` writes here by
# default (RUN_DIR), and everything under it stays out of the tree.
.verify-run/
